[{"id":"smq-year1-1.09-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>A rectangular garden is 30m by 40m. The path surrounding a rectangular pond has a consistent width of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and total area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"864\\text{m}^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the width and length of the pond.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.09/questions/assets/diagrams/q1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","steps":["<p>Length of pond: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"40-2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Width of pond: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30-2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Area of pond is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"30\\times40-864=336\\text{m}^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(40-2x)(30-2x)=336\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4x^2-140x+1200=336\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4x^2-140x+864=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x-8)(x-27)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=27\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  It can't physically be 27m so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=8\\text{m}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Length of pond: 24m  Width of pond: 14m</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.09-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>A room is comprised of two areas; one square with length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m, and one rectangular with width <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(x+2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m and length 10 m. It has a total area of 44 <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\text{m}^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2+10(x+2)=44\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow x^2+10x+20=44\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow x^2+10x-24=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore x=-12\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  It can't physically be <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-12\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.09-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>For the equations below, without manipulating the equation, state the number of real roots:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(x+1)^2+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-(x+1)^2+2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(x-4)^2-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-(x-4)^2-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(x+2)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Minimum at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so no real roots</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Maximum at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so 2 real roots</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Minimum at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,-3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so 2 real roots</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>Maximum at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,-3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so no real roots</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p>Minimum at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so 1 (repeated) real root</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.09-q4","number":4,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac34x(x-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq x\\leq4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the minimum of the curve.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0,y=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4,y=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0,x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.09/solutions/assets/diagrams/s4a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Minimum at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac12,y=-\\frac3{16}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.09-q5","number":5,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{22}{25}x(200-x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\leq x\\leq200\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the maximum of the curve.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0,x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=200\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.09/solutions/assets/diagrams/s5a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Maximum at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=100\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\frac{22}{25}\\times100\\times100=8800\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.09-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>Sketch the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=a(x-b)^2+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for constants <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in each of the cases below. Label where the curve intersects with the axes.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a&gt;0,b&gt;0,c&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a&gt;0,b&lt;0,c&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a&lt;0,b&gt;0,c&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a&lt;0,b&lt;0,c&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.09/solutions/assets/diagrams/s6a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.09/solutions/assets/diagrams/s6b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.09/solutions/assets/diagrams/s6c.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.09/solutions/assets/diagrams/s6d.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.09-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>For the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=a(x-b)^2+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constants, state the conditions for the graph to have a minimum in the top left quadrant and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-intercept to be positive.</p>","steps":["<p>Minimum: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Minimum to have <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-value <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Top left quadrant: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a&gt;0,b&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.09-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>For the graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=a(x-b)^2+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are constants, state the conditions for the graph to have a maximum in the top right quadrant and the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-intercept to be negative.</p>","steps":["<p>Maximum: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Maximum to have <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-value <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  Maximum to have <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-value <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a&lt;0,b&gt;0,c&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-intercept <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a(-b)^2+c&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ab^2+c&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore a&lt;0,b&gt;0,c&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ab^2+c&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.09-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>The graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^2+3x+k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant has a minimum with coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-\\frac32,-\\frac12)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the coordinates of where the curve intersects</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p></li><li><p>the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2+3x+k=(x+\\frac32)^2-(\\frac32)^2+k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-(\\frac32)^2+k=-\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac94+k=-\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=\\frac74\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  So it crosses the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac74\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore(0,\\frac74)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2+3x+\\frac74=0\\Rightarrow x=-\\frac32\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt2}2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore(-\\frac32+\\frac{\\sqrt2}2,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-\\frac32-\\frac{\\sqrt2}2,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.09-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>The graph of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x^2+4kx+k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is a constant has a maximum with coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the coordinates of the points where the curve intersects</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li><p>the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p></li><li><p>the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-x^2+4kx+k=-(x-2)^2+5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"=-(x^2-4x+4)+5=-x^2+4x+1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  So it crosses the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-axis at 1  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore(0,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-x^2+4x+1=0\\Rightarrow x=2\\pm\\sqrt5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore(2-\\sqrt5,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2+\\sqrt5,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.09-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>By completing the square, show that the solutions to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ax^2+bx+c=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}ax^2+bx+c&amp;=0\\\\a(x^2+\\frac bax+\\frac ca)&amp;=0\\\\x^2+\\frac bax+\\frac ca&amp;=0\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Complete the square:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}(x+\\frac b{2a})^2-(\\frac b{2a})^2+\\frac ca&amp;=0\\\\(x+\\frac b{2a})^2-\\frac{b^2}{4a^2}+\\frac{4ac}{4a^2}&amp;=0\\\\(x+\\frac b{2a})^2-\\frac{b^2-4ac}{4a^2}&amp;=0\\\\(x+\\frac b{2a})^2&amp;=\\frac{b^2-4ac}{4a^2}\\\\x+\\frac b{2a}&amp;=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{b^2-4ac}{4a^2}}\\\\x&amp;=-\\frac b{2a}\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}\\\\x&amp;=\\frac{-b\\pm\\sqrt{b^2-4ac}}{2a}\\text{ as req}\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.09-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>A curve has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2x^2+x+k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\\ne0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Given that the roots of the equation have a difference of 2.5, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac{-1\\pm\\sqrt{1-8k}}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{-1-\\sqrt{1-8k}}4+\\frac52=\\frac{-1+\\sqrt{1-8k}}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{9-\\sqrt{1-8k}}4=\\frac{-1+\\sqrt{1-8k}}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"9-\\sqrt{1-8k}=-1+\\sqrt{1-8k}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10=2\\sqrt{1-8k}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5=\\sqrt{1-8k}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"25=1-8k\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.09-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>A curve has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-5x^2-kx+3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\\ne0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Given that the roots of the equation have a difference of 1.6, find the possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac{k\\pm\\sqrt{k^2+60}}{-10}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{k-\\sqrt{k^2+60}}{-10}+1.6=\\frac{k+\\sqrt{k^2+60}}{-10}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{-16+k-\\sqrt{k^2+60}}{-10}=\\frac{k+\\sqrt{k^2+60}}{-10}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-16+k-\\sqrt{k^2+60}=k+\\sqrt{k^2+60}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-16=2\\sqrt{k^2+60}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-8=\\sqrt{k^2+60}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>  <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"64=k^2+60\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=\\pm2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]}]